sjdevnull@yahoo.com wrote:
>I think if you keep your level lower, there won't be archons.  For a
>valkyrie, there's no good reason to go above 14 unless you run short of
>weapon skill slots.

This is largely a misconception.  Archons are difficulty 26; if the
effective dungeon level is 51 or greater, it is absolutely impossible
to prevent the generation of Archons by suppressing your experience
level (since being drained to XL 0 causes you to die regardless of your
remaining hit points).  Furthermore...

Looking at Dylan's mon2-343.txt spoiler:
  For this purpose, once you have the Amulet of Yendor your dungeon
  level is considered to be that of the Sanctum, and in the endgame
  to be the depth of the Sanctum plus half your experience level.

To prevent Archon generation for various Sanctum depths, you would
therefore need to have the following experience level (or lower):
45 (4% chance) - XL 4
46 (8% chance) - XL 3
47 (12% chance) - XL 3
48 (16% chance) - XL 2
49 (20% chance) - XL 1
50 (16% chance) - XL 1
51 (12% chance) - XL 0 i.e. impossible.
52 (8% chance) - XL 0 i.e. impossible.
53 (4% chance) - XL -1 i.e. impossible.

Thus, there is a 24% chance that there is no way to prevent Archon
generation on the Astral Plane by draining your experience level, and
a 36% chance that you would need to be 1st level to prevent Archon
generation on the Astral Plane, and only a 4% chance that being 4th
level would suffice to prevent it.

So, in short:
1) You have to faff about with Stormbringer or wraiths or vampires to
   achieve the feat at all (since you can't win the game without spending
   at least a little time at XL 14).
2) There is a 24% chance that the feat is unachievable.
3) Achieving level 30 with a human valkyrie with Con 18 gets you an
   additional 96 hit points relative to your total at 14th level;
   further gain-level effects will give you another six HP each without 
   further increasing monster HP.  These numbers go up to 128 and eight
   respectively if you are a dwarven valkyrie with Con 20.

So, don't bother trying to suppress your experience level.  It really
isn't worth the bother.
